## Repeating Code with While Loops

Sometimes you need to do something over and over. A **while loop** runs a block of code repeatedly as long as a condition remains `true`.

### Basic While Loop

```xiom
var count = 0;
while count < 5 {
  io.println("Count is: " + count);
  count = count + 1;
}
// Prints: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4
```

The loop body executes repeatedly. Each time, it checks `count < 5`. When `count` reaches 5, the condition becomes `false` and the loop stops.

### Countdown Pattern

```xiom
var n = 10;
while n > 0 {
  io.println(n);
  n = n - 1;
}
io.println("Liftoff!");
```

### Break — Exit Early

Use `break` to jump out of a loop immediately:

```xiom
var i = 0;
while true {
  if i >= 10 { break; }
  i = i + 1;
}
// The loop exits when i reaches 10
```

`while true` creates an infinite loop — dangerous without a `break`!

### Continue — Skip an Iteration

Use `continue` to jump to the next iteration:

```xiom
var i = 0;
while i < 10 {
  i = i + 1;
  if i % 2 == 0 { continue; }  // skip even numbers
  io.println(i);                // only prints odds
}
```

### Common Pattern: Summing

```xiom
var i = 1;
var sum = 0;
while i <= 100 {
  sum = sum + i;
  i = i + 1;
}
// sum is now 5050 (sum of 1 to 100)
```

